# Eggs Benedict

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1018626-eggs-benedict) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250909054641/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1018626-eggs-benedict))

{ rating="4" image="eggs_benedict.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Benedict and Assembly

- [ ] 4 [english muffins]{ ing="english-muffins" }, split
- [ ] 8 slices [Canadian bacon]{ ing="canadian-bacon" } or thick-cut ham
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [chopped chives]{ ing="chopped-chives" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }
- [ ] [flaky sea salt]{ ing="flaky-sea-salt" }
- [ ] [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }

### Hollandaise Ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 cup (1 stick) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }
- [ ] 3 large [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" }
- [ ] 2 tsp fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } (1/4 lemon)
- [ ] 1/4 teaspoon [cayenne or hot paprika]{ ing="cayenne-or-hot-paprika" }
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, kosher
- [ ] [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }

### Poached Eggs

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [white distilled vinegar]{ ing="white-distilled-vinegar" }
- [ ] [salt]{ ing="salt" }, kosher
- [ ] 8 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] [egg poaching cups]{ ing="egg-poaching-cups" }, metal or silicone

## Recipe

### Prep

1. Melt [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, pour in glass juicer, prep lemon and cayenne in [cup]{ ing="egg-poaching-cups" } then check blender speed. Let cool slightly if using a plastic blender
1. Cut up fruit for side dish and prep table

### Make Hollandaise

1. Melt butter in a small pot over medium heat until it’s foamy but not yet beginning to brown, 3 to 4 minutes
1. Place [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" } and 2-3 tsp water in a blender. Start blending and very slowly add the hot, melted butter until incorporated then add the [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, cayenne, [salt]{ ing="flaky-sea-salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }
1. Transfer the hollandaise to a small bowl, and place plastic wrap directly on the surface so it doesn’t form a skin. Set aside at room temperature

### Toppings

1. _In parallel to the Hollandaise step…_
1. Cook [Canadian bacon]{ ing="canadian-bacon" } or ham (or bacon) in a medium skillet over medium–high heat until golden brown and just crisp at the edges, about 6 minutes.
1. Poach the [eggs]{ ing="egg" }:

   1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil, then reduce to low. Add 1 Tbsp of [vinegar]{ ing="white-distilled-vinegar" }
   1. Over a small bowl, crack the egg in a fine mesh sieve to let the liquidy part drain, then transfer the remaining yolk and white to a small bowl and pour into the pot
   1. Cook for 3 minutes and remove with a slotted spoon
1. Thoroughly toast the [English muffins]{ ing="english-muffins" } until crisp and golden brown–they will need to be sturdy

### Assemble

1. Butter the eight halves of English muffin on a plate and butter them generously. Top each with a slice of selected meat, poached egg, then spoon hollandaise sauce. Sprinkle with [chives]{ ing="chopped-chives" }, [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, flaky sea salt, and black pepper.

## Notes

1. The tricky part of this recipe is to get everything hot and served at the same time
